<title>USA: AMERCO buys back shrs under settlement.</title>
<headline>AMERCO buys back shrs under settlement.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX, Ariz. 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMERCO Inc, the holding company for U-Haul International Inc, said Friday it has purchased 2.02 million shares of its common stock from Katrina Carlson and Kattydid Inc as part of a settlement.</p>
<p>AMERCO paid about $13.7 million for the stock. It also paid Katrina Carlson, Kattydid's sole voting stockholder and the daughter of U-Haul founder L.S. Shoen, about $37 million.</p>
<p>The remaining settlement amount of about $102 million is to be paid by October 1, when an additional 4.04 million shares are to be repurchased.</p>
